CM_ "Message and signal names follow the tc275_freertos/dev-BYD_ATTO3 and local
BYD_Atto3 CANape convention (`{A|B|C|U}_0xNNN_Function_Ln_period`), not the
community shemps/byd-atto3-openpilot-port fork. Two exceptions are required by
opendbc/can/dbc.py:set_signal_type, which attaches counter/checksum semantics
by matching the literal signal names `COUNTER` and `CHECKSUM` — the canonical
per-message names (e.g. `MPC_RollingCounter_1E2`) cannot be used here. Fields
still under a community/reference-only name have not been confirmed bit-
identical against the local CANape/tc275 capture; see
nagaspilot/docs/BYD_REFERENCE_PARITY_AUDIT.md and
~/panda/BYD_Atto3/DOC/community_port_comparison.md before renaming them.";
CM_ BO_ 287 "EPS steering wheel angle + driver torque. Validated: angle range plausible, EPS_DriverTorque stays near 0 when hands-off.";
CM_ BO_ 290 "Per-wheel speed from ESP (FL/FR/BL/BR). Scale 0.1 kph/bit. Use ESP_VehicleSpeed (0x1F0) for the aggregated filtered value openpilot consumes.";
CM_ BO_ 307 "Turn signal / stalk info. Bit layout matches the tc275_freertos dev/BYD_ATTO3 firmware (DBC/byd_atto3.c, case 0x133), which reads BCM_TurnSignalStalk on the real car; the prior community LEFT_BLINKER/RIGHT_BLINKER bit-flag decode at a different bit position has been replaced.";
CM_ BO_ 482 "Lateral steering command sent by MPC camera/ADAS ECU to EPS. Blocked by panda on bus 2; panda injects its own on bus 0.";
CM_ BO_ 496 "Wheel speed (cleaned average). Validated: 0-127 km/h matching driving speed.";
CM_ BO_ 508 "Column steering torque from EPS. TORQUE_FAILED, DRIVER_TORQUE, TARGET_ANGLE, HANDS_ON_WHEEL_WARN and TORQUE_TEMP_FAILED have no confirmed counterpart in the local CANape capture; kept as community-sourced telemetry, not safety inputs.";
CM_ BO_ 578 "Drivetrain state: gear, brake pressed, raw throttle. Bit layout (RAW_THROTTLE 24|7, VCU_BrakePressed 37|1, VCU_Gear 40|3, all Intel) matches the tc275_freertos dev/BYD_ATTO3 firmware (DBC/byd_atto3.c, case 0x242).";
CM_ BO_ 660 "Body/meter cluster: doors + seatbelt. Bit layout confirmed against the tc275_freertos dev/BYD_ATTO3 firmware (DBC/byd_atto3.c, case 0x294); all fields Intel.";
CM_ BO_ 790 "LKAS HUD ADAS message from camera. Blocked by panda on bus 2; panda re-injects. MPC_HandsOnWheelRequest, MPC_LkasActive and MPC_LkasState are firmware-confirmed (DBC/byd_atto3.c, case 0x316); the firmware also reads an undocumented bit 35 (handsOffDetected) that overlaps MPC_RightLaneState's low bit — not yet reconciled. AUTO_LIGHT, HMA_ON_OFF and LDSW_TYPE still use a different bit offset/endianness with no firmware witness and are kept unrenamed. HudPt1-4 name previously-unnamed bits so a decode/repack round-trips byte-exact: the modules validate this frame's full bit pattern and fail-safe (latched DTCs) if a regenerated frame flips any bit. On-car MPC_HudPt3 bit 32 is constant 1; an unnamed bit packs as 0.";
CM_ BO_ 813 "ACC HUD ADAS message (cruise set speed, distance, ACC state). VCU_ACCSetSpeed, VCU_ACCSetDistance and VCU_ACCState are firmware-confirmed (DBC/byd_atto3.c, case 0x32D); the secondary ACC_ON1/ACC_ON2 flags are not read by that firmware and remain unconfirmed.";
CM_ BO_ 814 "ACC acceleration command from ADAS ECU. Blocked by panda on bus 2 when OP longitudinal active. Bit layout firmware-confirmed (DBC/byd_atto3.c, case 0x32E TX) except SET_ME_XF, which that code does not write.";
CM_ BO_ 834 "Gas/brake pedal state. Bit layout and raw (unscaled) unit match the tc275_freertos dev/BYD_ATTO3 firmware (DBC/byd_atto3.c, case 0x342); VCU_AccelPedalRaw > 10 is the tested gas-pressed threshold (also used raw in opendbc/safety/modes/byd.h). Percent/normalized conversion is applied downstream in carstate.py, not in this scale.";
CM_ BO_ 944 "Steering-wheel cruise control buttons. Bit layout matches the tc275_freertos dev/BYD_ATTO3 firmware (DBC/byd_atto3.c, case 0x3B0), which only decodes SWC_CruiseScrollDirection, SWC_LCCButton and SWC_CruiseSetButton on the real car; the prior community SET_BTN/RES_BTN/LKAS_ON_BTN/distance-button fields were unvalidated and have been dropped.";
CM_ BO_ 1048 "Blind-spot approach state. Bit layout (VCU_BSDLeftApproach 8|2, VCU_BSDRightApproach 10|2, VCU_BSDApproach 17|1, all Intel) matches the tc275_freertos dev/BYD_ATTO3 firmware (DBC/byd_atto3.c, case 0x418).";
VAL_ 307 BCM_TurnSignalStalk 0 "OFF" 1 "LEFT" 2 "RIGHT";
VAL_ 508 TORQUE_TEMP_FAILED 1 "TooLarge" 2 "TooFast" 3 "Both";
VAL_ 578 VCU_Gear 4 "D" 2 "R" 3 "N" 1 "P";
VAL_ 790 AUTO_LIGHT 1 "OFF" 2 "ON";
VAL_ 790 MPC_LeftLaneState 0 "OFF" 1 "GREEN" 2 "ORANGE";
VAL_ 790 MPC_LksMode 0 "OFF" 1 "DIVERGE" 2 "KEEPING" 3 "ALL";
VAL_ 790 MPC_TjaIcaState 0 "OFF" 1 "PASSIVE" 2 "ACTIVE1" 3 "ACTIVE2" 4 "FAULT";
VAL_ 790 MPC_SlaState 0 "OFF" 1 "FUSION_MODE" 2 "VISION_MODE" 3 "NV_ONLY_MODE" 4 "DEFECT";
VAL_ 790 MPC_RightLaneState 0 "OFF" 1 "GREEN" 2 "ORANGE";
VAL_ 790 MPC_LkasState 2 "ACTIVE" 1 "OFF";
VAL_ 790 LDSW_TYPE 0 "VIBRATE" 1 "SOUND" 2 "ALL";
VAL_ 813 VCU_ACCSetDistance 4 "4bar" 3 "3bar" 2 "2bar" 1 "1bar";
VAL_ 813 VCU_ACCState 0 "OFF" 2 "ACC_ON" 3 "ACC_ACTIVE" 5 "FORCE_ACCEL" 7 "ERROR";
